"""The checks of the webhooks: the signatures and the IDs of the events (ADR 0028).

A webhook endpoint reads the raw body, checks its signature with the
secret of the webhook, and keeps the ID of the event in the table
`webhook_events`. The ID is unique for each webhook, so a repeated
delivery of an event does not run the logic again. The row and the
changes of the logic go into the same transaction: when the logic fails,
the sender can deliver the event again.
"""

{{ py.imports(
